{"uid":"scripts/broadcom_wps_drive.sh","name":"broadcom_wps_drive.sh","qualname":"scripts/broadcom_wps_drive.sh","kind":"module","file":"scripts/broadcom_wps_drive.sh","line":1,"end_line":422,"language":"sh","signature":"","params":[],"returns":"","decorators":[],"bases":[],"modifiers":[],"visibility":"public","doc":{"summary":"broadcom_wps_drive.sh - operator-side driver for the Broadcom 802.11 SDK detection toolkit.","description":"The upstream project ships two detectors: a live fingerprinter that tells Broadcom's vulnerable wps_monitor apart from a patched hostapd, and YARA rules for extracted firmware. The live path needs a monitor-mode adapter, root privileges and scapy, and it leaves the adapter in monitor mode. This driver owns that operational overhead:  doctor       report the toolchain, the adapter and the configured SSID monitor      put the adapter in monitor mode unmonitor    restore the adapter to managed mode fingerprint  run the live detector and archive the verdict yara         run the upstream rules against an extracted firmware tree status       report the current state without touching the radio  Usage: broadcom_wps_drive.sh doctor broadcom_wps_drive.sh monitor broadcom_wps_drive.sh unmonitor broadcom_wps_drive.sh fingerprint broadcom_wps_drive.sh yara <firmware-dir> broadcom_wps_drive.sh status  Flags (after the action): --ssid <ssid>        access point to fingerprint --interface <iface>  wireless adapter to use --target <dir>       firmware tree for the YARA pass --keep-monitor       leave the adapter in monitor mode after the run --debug-assoc        log 802.11 auth status codes (passed to the tool)","params":[],"returns":null,"yields":null,"raises":[],"attributes":[],"examples":[],"notes":[],"see_also":[],"deprecated":"","since":"","style":"plain"},"parent":"","members":["scripts/broadcom_wps_drive.sh::log","scripts/broadcom_wps_drive.sh::warn","scripts/broadcom_wps_drive.sh::die","scripts/broadcom_wps_drive.sh::usage","scripts/broadcom_wps_drive.sh::payload_value","scripts/broadcom_wps_drive.sh::parse_flags","scripts/broadcom_wps_drive.sh::detect_interface","scripts/broadcom_wps_drive.sh::is_wireless","scripts/broadcom_wps_drive.sh::apply_interface","scripts/broadcom_wps_drive.sh::resolve_interface","scripts/broadcom_wps_drive.sh::is_root","scripts/broadcom_wps_drive.sh::have_sudo","scripts/broadcom_wps_drive.sh::elevate","scripts/broadcom_wps_drive.sh::interface_mode","scripts/broadcom_wps_drive.sh::interface_up","scripts/broadcom_wps_drive.sh::python_bin","scripts/broadcom_wps_drive.sh::has_scapy","scripts/broadcom_wps_drive.sh::do_monitor","scripts/broadcom_wps_drive.sh::do_unmonitor","scripts/broadcom_wps_drive.sh::ensure_monitor_mode","scripts/broadcom_wps_drive.sh::run_fingerprint","scripts/broadcom_wps_drive.sh::run_yara","scripts/broadcom_wps_drive.sh::do_status","scripts/broadcom_wps_drive.sh::do_doctor","scripts/broadcom_wps_drive.sh::main"],"inferred_raises":[],"returns_value":null,"value":"","base_uids":[],"subclasses":[],"calls":[],"called_by":[]}
